From c425cf7c95eb033a8260d8437c71b233a4fcacd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akshat Srivastava <akshat.sanya@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:37:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Server-side turn timer with automatic turn end and countdown
 display

- Every turn (heroes and DM) has a time limit; when it runs out the SERVER ends the turn,
  exactly like End turn (a DM's orders given so far are still carried out)
- Limits come from rules.json: heroTurnTimeLimitSeconds (now 60) and new
  dmTurnTimeLimitSeconds (60, optional - defaults to the hero value)
- Timer restarts on every turn change (End turn, timeout, skipped players, computer DM);
  playing a card does not give extra time
- New 'info' message tells the room when a turn timed out
- State sends turnSeconds and turnMsLeft; the client counts down from its own clock,
  so client and server clocks don't need to match
- Battle screen: countdown bar next to End turn (green / orange <= 20 s / red <= 10 s,
  'Hurry!' for the active player) and the timeout message
- dungeon_server <port> <data> <seconds> overrides the limit for demos
- net_tests: countdown sent to everyone, turn not ended early, timeout message,
  fresh timer for the next player, computer DM after timeouts, no extra time for
  playing a card, DM timed too, DM's orders carried out on timeout
